@if (Visible)
{
    <div class="modal fade show d-block" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" @onclick="OnClose">
        <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-scrollable" role="document" @onclick:stopPropagation>
            <div class="modal-content">
                <div class="modal-header">
                    <h5 class="modal-title">How Commander Discovery works</h5>
                    <button type="button" class="btn-close" @onclick="OnClose"></button>
                </div>
                <div class="modal-body">

                    <p class="text-muted">
                        Discovery helps you find a commander when you know what kind of deck you want to build
                        but haven't settled on who should lead it.
                    </p>

                    <h6 class="fw-semibold mt-3">Two pathways</h6>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Guided</strong> lets you select archetypes (how the deck wins) and themes
                        (what it does mechanically), plus optional filters for color identity, power bracket,
                        and budget. The tool matches commanders against these structured criteria.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Custom</strong> lets you describe your strategy in prose instead — useful when
                        your idea doesn't fit neatly into preset categories or when you want to be more specific
                        about play patterns and win conditions.
                    </p>

                    <h6 class="fw-semibold mt-3">1. Commander pool</h6>
                    <p>
                        All legal commanders from Scryfall's card database are the starting candidate pool.
                        If you set a color identity filter, only commanders matching those exact colors are kept.
                        Bracket and budget filters narrow the pool further before scoring begins.
                    </p>

                    <h6 class="fw-semibold mt-3">2. AI scoring <span class="badge bg-secondary fw-normal ms-1" style="font-size: 0.7em;">AI step</span></h6>
                    <p>
                        Your chosen model ranks commanders against your criteria using EDHREC data for each
                        candidate. This is where the reasoning level you selected matters — the AI evaluates
                        how well each commander's abilities and typical play patterns align with your strategy,
                        and writes a rationale for each suggestion explaining the fit.
                    </p>

                    <h6 class="fw-semibold mt-3">3. Results</h6>
                    <p>
                        Each suggestion shows the commander's card art, oracle text, a written rationale, and
                        the top popular themes from EDHREC for that commander — ranked by how many EDHREC decks
                        use them. Blue badges are themes and archetypes the app recognises; grey badges are
                        EDHREC-specific tags without a direct app equivalent.
                    </p>
                    <p class="mb-0">
                        Clicking a suggestion jumps to the Commander Builder with that commander pre-selected.
                        If you haven't chosen a theme yourself, the builder link automatically presets the top
                        known EDHREC theme as a starting point.
                    </p>

                    <hr class="my-3" />

                    <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
                        <strong>Partner pairs</strong> are fully supported — both halves of a partner pair
                        are evaluated together, and recommendations are drawn from both EDHREC partner endpoints.
                    </p>

                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="modal-backdrop fade show"></div>
}
